<article class="page-container">
  <div class="page-card">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; Resources</p>
    <h1>Photography Privacy Policy Template (Free Sample)</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Updated October 23, 2026</p>

    <p>A photography privacy policy template is a ready-made policy you edit with your own business details. The free sample below covers what photographers actually handle: client and booking data, model releases, EXIF and geotag metadata, gallery and proofing platforms, print labs, payment processors, and raw-file retention. Copy it, replace the bracketed text, and delete anything that doesn't match how you work.</p>

    <nav class="toc">
      <p class="toc-title">Contents</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sample-template">Sample Photography Privacy Policy Template</a></li>
        <li><a href="#customize">How to Customize the Template</a></li>
        <li><a href="#photography-clauses">Clauses Generic Templates Miss</a></li>
        <li><a href="#privacy-laws">Which Privacy Laws Apply to Photographers</a></li>
        <li><a href="#where-to-display">Where to Display Your Privacy Policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="sample-template">Sample Photography Privacy Policy Template</h2>

    <p>Fill in or choose between the bracketed options, and delete sections that don't apply, such as print labs or second shooters.</p>

    <div class="copy-block">
      <div class="copy-block-header">
        <span class="copy-block-label">Sample Photography Privacy Policy — ready to copy</span>
      </div>
      <div class="copy-block-body" id="sample-policy-text">
<p><strong>Privacy Policy for [Your Photography Business Name]</strong></p>
<p><em>Last updated: [Date]</em></p>

<p><strong>1. Who We Are</strong></p>
<p>[Your Photography Business Name] ("we," "us," or "our") is a photography business based in [City, Country] that operates [yourwebsite.com]. This policy explains what personal data we collect when you visit our website, book a session, or appear in our photographs, and how we use, share, and keep it.</p>

<p><strong>2. Information We Collect</strong></p>
<p><em>Contact and booking details.</em> When you send an inquiry or book a session, we collect your name, email address, phone number, and details of your shoot, such as the date, location, session type, and any notes you share. For weddings and events, this can include venue addresses, timelines, and the names of family members or guests you give us.</p>
<p><em>Model release and consent records.</em> If you sign a model release, we keep your name, signature, the date, and the uses you agreed to. For minors, a parent or guardian signs the release, and we keep their details too.</p>
<p><em>Photographs and image metadata.</em> Photographs of identifiable people are personal data. Image files also contain EXIF metadata, which can include the date, camera details, and GPS coordinates of where a photo was taken. We remove location data from images we publish online. Files delivered to your private gallery [keep / do not keep] their original metadata.</p>
<p><em>Gallery and proofing activity.</em> When you use your online gallery, [gallery platform] records your email address, the images you view, favorite, download, or order, and technical details such as your IP address and device.</p>
<p><em>Payment information.</em> Deposits, invoices, and print orders are paid through [payment processor]. We receive payment confirmations and billing details, but we do not see or store your full card number.</p>
<p><em>Website usage data.</em> Our website uses [essential cookies only / analytics cookies from [analytics provider]] to understand how visitors use the site. [If applicable: We also use [Meta Pixel / Google Ads tag] to measure our advertising.]</p>

<p><strong>3. How We Use Your Information</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>To answer inquiries, schedule sessions, and manage our contract with you</li>
<li>To take payments and keep accounting records</li>
<li>To edit and deliver your photographs and fulfil print and album orders</li>
<li>To keep proof of the consent given in model releases</li>
<li>To show images in our portfolio, website, or social media only where you have agreed to this</li>
<li>To send newsletters or offers, only if you opted in</li>
</ul>
<p>Where the GDPR or UK GDPR applies, our legal bases are: performing our contract with you (bookings, delivery, payment), legal obligation (tax records), consent (marketing emails, non-essential cookies, portfolio use where consent is required), and legitimate interests (running and securing our business).</p>

<p><strong>4. Who We Share Your Information With</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Gallery and proofing platform:</strong> [Pixieset / ShootProof / Pic-Time / SmugMug] hosts your galleries and processes gallery orders.</li>
<li><strong>Print lab:</strong> [Lab name] receives the images you order and the name and shipping address needed to produce and deliver prints and albums.</li>
<li><strong>Payment processor:</strong> [Stripe / PayPal / Square] processes your payments.</li>
<li><strong>Booking and client management:</strong> [HoneyBook / Dubsado / Studio Ninja] stores inquiries, contracts, and invoices.</li>
<li><strong>Cloud storage and backup:</strong> [Google Drive / Dropbox / Backblaze] stores raw and edited files.</li>
<li><strong>Email and analytics:</strong> [Mailchimp / Flodesk] and [Google Analytics].</li>
<li><strong>Second shooters and editors:</strong> [If used] contractors who receive only the files and details needed for their work.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your personal information. We may disclose information if the law requires it.</p>

<p><strong>5. How Long We Keep Your Information</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Inquiries that do not lead to a booking: [12 months]</li>
<li>Contracts, invoices, and booking records: [6 years], for tax and accounting purposes</li>
<li>Raw (unedited) files: [12 months] after delivery, then deleted</li>
<li>Edited images: in your online gallery for [12 months], and in our archive for [X years] so we can help with lost files or reprints</li>
<li>Model releases: for as long as we use the images, plus [3 years]</li>
<li>Marketing list: until you unsubscribe</li>
</ul>
<p>You can ask us to delete your files and data sooner, unless the law requires us to keep them.</p>

<p><strong>6. Children</strong></p>
<p>Our website is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their personal information online. We photograph minors only with a parent or guardian's consent, and the parent or guardian may contact us at any time to access or delete their child's images and data.</p>

<p><strong>7. Your Privacy Rights</strong></p>
<p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or receive a copy of your personal data, to object to or restrict how we use it, and to withdraw consent at any time, including consent to portfolio or social media use of your images. Withdrawing consent does not undo uses already made, such as printed materials. If you are in the EU or UK, you can also complain to your local data protection authority. To make a request, email [your-email@example.com]. We respond within one month.</p>

<p><strong>8. Security and International Transfers</strong></p>
<p>We protect your data with password-protected galleries, secured accounts, and encrypted backups. Where providers store data outside your country, they use legally required safeguards such as standard contractual clauses.</p>

<p><strong>9. Changes to This Policy</strong></p>
<p>We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date above shows when it last changed.</p>

<p><strong>10. Contact Us</strong></p>
<p>[Your Photography Business Name]<br />[your-email@example.com]<br />[Business address]</p>
      </div>
